From 623f3838c27d08aab88f1e6f0f42ded2078e55c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:41:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] target/microblaze: truncate in fint

LOCAL ONLY: not for submission to qemu-devel (QEMU AI policy).
Reference for a hand-written fix.

UG984 describes fint as "a 32-bit truncating signed conversion", but
helper_fint uses float32_to_int32, which rounds in the current
rounding mode, round-to-nearest-even here because the FSR has no
rounding-mode field.  fint of 2.5 gives 2 and of 2.75 gives 3, where
the hardware gives 2 for both; -2.75 gives -3 rather than -2.

Use float32_to_int32_round_to_zero, as C's float-to-int conversion
does.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/microblaze/op_helper.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/microblaze/op_helper.c b/target/microblaze/op_helper.c
index 91abb2dea..c7c1ce67e 100644
--- a/target/microblaze/op_helper.c
+++ b/target/microblaze/op_helper.c
@@ -344,7 +344,7 @@ uint32_t helper_fint(CPUMBState *env, uint32_t a)
 
     set_float_exception_flags(0, &env->fp_status);
     fa.l = a;
-    r = float32_to_int32(fa.f, &env->fp_status);
+    r = float32_to_int32_round_to_zero(fa.f, &env->fp_status);
     flags = get_float_exception_flags(&env->fp_status);
     update_fpu_flags(env, flags, GETPC());
 
